# See https://www.dartlang.org/guides/libraries/private-files
# Flutter/Dart/Pub related
**/doc/api/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.packages
.pub-cache/
.pub/
build/
.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# If you're building an application, you may want to check-in your pubspec.lock
pubspec.lock
pubspec_overrides.yaml

# ...with one exception. The rollout matrix's control arm pins the last
# released at_client, and a control that re-resolves its transitive set on
# every machine is not a control: a changed result could be a finding or a
# different at_commons, with no way to tell which. Its lockfile is the pin.
# See docs/projects/pq/decisions.md 96 ruling 2.
!/tests/pq_matrix/published/pubspec.lock

# Avoid committing generated Javascript files:
*.dart.js
*.info.json      # Produced by the --dump-info flag.
*.js             # When generated by dart2js. Don't specify *.js if your
*.DS_Store                 # project includes source files written in JavaScript.
*.js_
*.js.deps
*.js.map

# IntelliJ related
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
*.idea/

# Visual Studio Code
.vscode/

# Codecov related

coverage/

# Functional test related

hive/

# Misc
.DS_Store

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include poetry.lock in version control.
#   This is especially recommended for binary packages to ensure reproducibility, and is more
#   commonly ignored for libraries.
#   https://python-poetry.org/docs/basic-usage/#commit-your-poetrylock-file-to-version-control
poetry.lock

# Miscellaneous
*.class
*.log
*.pyc
*.swp
.atom/
.buildlog/
.history
.svn/

# Android related
**/android/**/gradle-wrapper.jar
**/android/.gradle
**/android/captures/
**/android/gradlew
**/android/gradlew.bat
**/android/local.properties
**/android/**/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java

